  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Jack writes down a number with multiple digits.\nThe ratio of even digits in the number to the total number of digits is $1:3.$\nIf the number has $7$ even digits, how many odd digits are there?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $1:3$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of even digits, and the denominator represents the total number of digits.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $7$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 7}{3\\times 7}=\\frac{7}{21}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $21$ digits in total. \nSo, the number of odd digits in the number is\n\n$$\n21-7=14.\n$$",
